  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_38fe417801864fc7837a19ed5180001f",
      "statement": "The Spring OpenProject MCP Server is a Java 25 application built on Spring Boot 4.1.1 with Spring AI 2.0.1 that exposes an MCP server for managing OpenProject work packages, acting as a thin proxy between MCP clients and the OpenProject REST API (/api/v3).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://pom.xml#L14-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d289e41599f3138e78e5c55281a0c1c29bf32242fd471f2d16cd4cbf89e05bab:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://pom.xml#L38-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ab397018a8b80e34451b3199f920806598846d676203d6abb11ceee6177f1fab:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/de/tklein/tklab/openproject/mcp/SpringOpenprojectMcpServerApplication.java",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:235eddb97bc0a9ed51dc55eaa61c701738b8b5eda54ad21f61997f6aeb75bd0b"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6e38e770f32e4e329f52676974f99174",
      "statement": "The server supports two MCP transport protocols configurable via spring.ai.mcp.server.protocol: SSE (GET /sse for server-to-client streaming, POST /mcp for client-to-server) and STREAMABLE (single bidirectional endpoint at /mcp). The two protocols cannot be bound simultaneously because the transport defines the wiring, endpoints, and message routing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://pom.xml#L131-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2a0e44d9596caf79ddec86ccf061ca64e879f92789cba137791d731dd80909ce:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/resources/application.properties#L21-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48b0313b8c12813599d9f10a68cbbafebd2c67402aa08b351368e0b5107c841d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f3a0583783c9428c877a45de880818d4",
      "statement": "The application runs on port 8080 with a separate management (actuator) port at 8081.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/resources/application.properties#L3-L4",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dcbb5b3ddd80e4d8341c4c8a9588cfa8b13325324caf4c8a91c6ee02e9672af6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fada18adadc74e379203da7fb81b5837",
      "statement": "Authentication uses a two-layer approach: McpBearerAuthenticationFilter extracts the Authorization: Bearer header from MCP requests to /mcp and /sse, then OpenProjectTokenValidator validates the token by calling OpenProjectApiClient.root() (/api/v3 endpoint). The validated bearer token is converted to OpenProject's Basic auth format (apikey:<token>) by OpenProjectAuthHeaderFactory for all outbound HTTP requests.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/de/tklein/tklab/openproject/mcp/openproject/client/OpenProjectAuthHeaderFactory.java",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:2e584bd921739068a22082fc6336f70b67b9aab35d5f9b1eefdedc83453420e8"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/de/tklein/tklab/openproject/mcp/security/McpBearerAuthenticationFilter.java",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:3996e945fb43d4496d07d77aaac26182fade71f750e75b935328fc69d45140d8"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/de/tklein/tklab/openproject/mcp/security/OpenProjectTokenValidator.java",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:e75ec6276d60ee6eff5e70c16cafe74ae29cc5c7bb3a1dad78af4e2fbec9a876"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e500abcd6d1241819337e2212f6cb867",
      "statement": "Token validation results are cached in a Caffeine-backed store with a 60-minute TTL. The raw token is never stored in the cache; only its SHA-256 hash (of baseUrl|token) serves as the cache key.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/de/tklein/tklab/openproject/mcp/security/OpenProjectTokenValidationCache.java",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:463691a95d56452e92b00608609c20d3615cdda4607b3ed363f2f5ec49ec44d9"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/de/tklein/tklab/openproject/mcp/security/OpenProjectTokenValidator.java#L38-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:111e9c534330eccf3040349fd07ed0b0cb5f356d6515a625485118c66a583859:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/resources/application.properties#L8-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:655c29003ecba11e1e2633ec12f069dc9c0044d59b1bfe217b235e7c351e8c52:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_391c66a99f364f1eb5c532b0773f1102",
      "statement": "The OpenProjectConnectionResolver interface abstracts how the OpenProject base URL and bearer token are obtained. The active implementation HttpHeaderOpenProjectConnectionResolver reads the base URL from the openproject.url property (default https://localhost) or the X-OpenProject-Base-Url header when openproject.allow-header-base-url=true. A secondary EnvOpenProjectConnectionResolver exists but is commented out, providing an environment-variable-based alternative.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/de/tklein/tklab/openproject/mcp/openproject/client/EnvOpenProjectConnectionResolver.java",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:321d88c5375d4f1d9b9108070643ba600b959a06d2c2f636c00fd70d18a84d51"
        },
